# Synapse Context Compiler — .clinerules
# Drop this in the project root. Cline reads it at session start.

## Tech stack & versions
- Go 1.22+
- sqlite-vec v0.1.x (github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec-go-bindings)
- onnxruntime-go v1.x (github.com/yalue/onnxruntime_go) — all-MiniLM-L6-v2 ONNX
- tiktoken-go v0.x (github.com/pkoukk/tiktoken-go)
- chi v5 (github.com/go-chi/chi/v5) — HTTP router for REST API
- go-yaml v3 (gopkg.in/yaml.v3) — config parsing
- testify v1 (github.com/stretchr/testify) — assertions
- Node.js (none — no JS build pipeline; web UI is single-file vanilla HTML/JS)

## Folder structure
synapse/
├── cmd/
│   └── synapse/
│       └── main.go          # Binary entrypoint, flag parsing
├── internal/
│   ├── proxy/               # Reverse proxy handler, request interception
│   ├── classifier/          # Intent classifier (TF-IDF + keyword rules)
│   ├── scorer/              # 4-Factor Sieve — S, R, I, T computation
│   ├── store/               # sqlite-vec memory store, embedding write/read
│   ├── embedder/            # ONNX embedding model wrapper + OpenAI fallback
│   ├── dedup/               # Cosine deduplication pass
│   ├── budget/              # tiktoken-go token counter + greedy fill
│   ├── compiler/            # Assembles compiled messages[] + Trace manifest
│   ├── api/                 # REST API handlers (chi router)
│   └── config/              # YAML config loader + defaults
├── ui/
│   └── index.html           # Single-file trace inspector (vanilla HTML/JS)
├── schemas/
│   └── memory-trace.schema.json  # Published JSON Schema for trace output
├── testdata/                # Sample sessions for benchmark tests
├── .clinerules              # This file
├── synapse.yaml.example     # Annotated example config
└── README.md

## Coding style
- async patterns: use goroutines + channels, not callbacks
- functional over stateful structs where practical — pure functions for scoring
- camelCase for unexported, PascalCase for exported; kebab-case for config keys
- max 300 lines per file — split by responsibility if approaching limit
- interfaces for every external dependency (store, embedder, classifier) — enables mocking in tests
- no global state — pass config/deps via constructor injection
- comments on all exported types and functions; inline comments only for non-obvious logic

## Error handling
- always wrap errors: `fmt.Errorf("scorer: %w", err)`
- return errors up the stack — do not log + swallow
- top-level handlers log at ERROR level and return 500 with a sanitized message (never leak internals)
- use slog (stdlib) for structured logging — no third-party logger
- startup validation: if config is invalid, log.Fatal with clear message — no silent defaults that hide misconfiguration
- never log Authorization headers or bearer tokens at any log level

## Guardrails
- do not install new dependencies without asking — the binary size and single-binary goal matter
- do not touch files outside the current phase's scope
- no hardcoded secrets, API keys, or localhost URLs — everything via config or env
- do not refactor working code from a prior phase unless a bug requires it
- Authorization headers must NEVER appear in log output — this is a security requirement, not a preference
- proxy default binding is 127.0.0.1 — never change default to 0.0.0.0
- all config files written by Synapse must be created with 0600 permissions
- Memory Trace JSON is in-memory only by default; persistence requires explicit --persist-traces flag